## 1. Executive Summary

This project detects cyber intrusions, reconstructs how they spread through a network, and — through its novel **Precog Engine** — forecasts where an attacker is most likely to go next and lets an analyst pre-emptively stop them, before the next step happens. It combines four subjects into one working product: an ML detection pipeline, a live 3D computer-graphics visualization of the attack, a mobile app for on-the-go alerting and one-tap containment, and a closed feedback loop that re-evaluates the situation after every response.

The system operates in **Replay Mode**: rather than running live attacks against real virtual machines, it replays realistic, pre-recorded attack event sequences (built from the CICIDS2017 dataset and scripted to resemble real attack-tool output) through the exact same live pipeline a real attack would trigger. This was a deliberate decision (Section 7) to keep the project achievable for a team with no prior networking, Linux, or cybersecurity background, while preserving the full "live, reactive dashboard" demo experience.

