## 3. Existing Systems & Gap Analysis

| Existing System | Category | What It Does | Limitation |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Bitdefender GravityZone** | Endpoint Detection & Response | Detects and reports malicious activity on endpoints | Purely descriptive/reactive — reports what happened, does not forecast what happens next |
| **CrowdStrike Falcon** | Endpoint Detection & Response | Real-time endpoint monitoring and incident response | Same limitation — strong at detection and response, not at predicting the attacker's next move |
| **Sekoia.io** | Attack-Path Visualization | Visualizes attack paths and relationships between security events | Visualization is after-the-fact; shows the graph once compromise is already detected, not before |

**The gap:** every tool in this category answers *"what happened?"* None of them attempt live, node-level, confidence-scored forecasting of the attacker's next move combined with an actionable pre-emptive containment step that closes back into the same live system. That closed loop — **detect → forecast → act → re-evaluate** — is the specific gap this project targets, not a prettier version of an already-solved graph-visualization problem.

