## 12. Legal, Ethical & Safety Boundaries

Because this project uses **Replay Mode** rather than a live attack lab, its legal and ethical footprint is minimal by design: no scanning, exploitation, or attack tool is ever run against a live network, a classmate's device, or any infrastructure the team does not fully own. All attack behavior in this project is represented as pre-recorded dataset traffic or scripted event logs — never as a live action against real infrastructure. This will be stated explicitly in the paper's methodology section.

Additional safeguards carried through the design:

- Containment actions are simulated (a status change plus a logged action), never real network enforcement against a live system.
- No secrets, credentials, or real personal data are used anywhere in the pipeline — only CICIDS2017 (a licensed public research dataset) and internally generated replay logs.
- Human confirmation is required before any containment action executes; nothing acts autonomously without an analyst's tap.

