## 13. Expected Outcomes & Success Criteria

By the end of the semester, the project should be able to demonstrate:

- A working end-to-end pipeline: replayed event → detection → attack-path graph → ATT&CK context → Precog forecast → 3D visualization → mobile alert → analyst containment → re-evaluation.
- Measured (not assumed) detection performance on a held-out portion of CICIDS2017, reported with precision, recall, F1, and false-positive rate.
- A working Precog Engine with its own reported forecast accuracy for the demo session.
- A functioning installable mobile web app (PWA per Section 11; APK only if required) receiving live alerts and executing a containment action.
- A rehearsed, reliable golden-path demo, with a recorded backup video.
- An IEEE-formatted paper scoped specifically around the Precog Engine's forecasting contribution, with an honest literature-search-backed novelty claim.

