## 15. Conclusion

This project takes a well-understood problem category (intrusion detection and attack-path visualization) and adds a genuinely closed-loop, forward-looking capability — the Precog Engine — that existing commercial and open-source tools do not attempt. By reusing best-in-class open-source repositories for every subsystem that already has one, adopting Replay Mode to keep the build achievable for a team with no prior background in the domain, and dividing the remaining work into four evenly balanced, technically coherent role groups, the project is scoped to be fully demoable, fully evaluable, and fully extensible into future semesters — while remaining honest, at every stage, about what it does and does not claim to do.
